1
00:01:31,909 --> 00:01:33,600
Look at Kanna.

2
00:01:33,849 --> 00:01:36,160
It smells so sweet and delicious from somewhere.

3
00:01:36,769 --> 00:01:38,200
No matter what you do, you'll never be able to.

4
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:40,880
And why... Next.

5
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,520
Please ask carefully.

6
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:52,400
She's always, always so delicious.

7
00:01:54,400 --> 00:02:00,400
I could just keep eating this forever... It's so good! It's delicious!

8
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:01,660
Drink up!

9
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:04,140
Come again!

10
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:11,860
Wait!

11
00:02:16,719 --> 00:02:18,140
You think I'll let you get away?!

12
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:27,720
Aaaah! What the hell? You ruined my candy!

13
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:34,980
I saw you! You're a thief! Shut up, you brat!

14
00:02:37,394 --> 00:02:39,420
I'm an oak tree puppet!

15
00:02:39,670 --> 00:02:41,480
Bruno, what are you doing?

16
00:02:41,634 --> 00:02:42,980
Oh, Papa!

17
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:54,560
He called me a thief!

18
00:02:55,010 --> 00:02:57,380
I saw you steal that candy!

19
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:02,840
The one who gets robbed is the real fool.

20
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:06,940
But stealing from other people is wrong!

21
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:10,980
You say you're an oak tree puppet?

22
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:17,220
A talking puppet? Now that's something you don't see every day.

23
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:21,240
Who made you?

24
00:03:21,429 --> 00:03:22,620
Grandpa did.

25
00:03:23,524 --> 00:03:24,524
Grandpa?

26
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:26,500
Hm?

27
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:37,260
Ah, do you really want to become a human that badly?

28
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:41,760
Of course I do! I want to eat chocolate and candy just like everyone else.

29
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,420
Delicious!

30
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:50,420
By the way, misters, what are you doing in a place like this?

31
00:03:50,785 --> 00:03:52,120
Earning a living.

32
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:53,220
Doing what?

33
00:03:57,154 --> 00:03:58,740
Look, they're back.

34
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:02,860
Boss, here's today's take.

35
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:04,580
Here, hand it over.

36
00:04:06,219 --> 00:04:08,900
Yeah, not bad. You guys can eat, too.

37
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:16,300
Yeah. We tried to kidnap some kids, but they're pretty cautious and wouldn't come near us.

38
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:18,959
Damn kids are getting too smart these days.

39
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:21,899
Oh, are you guys gypsies?

40
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:29,180
That's right. When we find a foolish kid, we snatch them up and sell them cheap to anyone who wants one.

41
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:31,340
I-I-I'm going home!

42
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:32,780
Hold on!

43
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:40,700
Don't worry, we're not gonna kidnap you. There's no point in kidnapping a wooden puppet.

44
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,420
You said your name was Mokku, right?

45
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:45,660
How'd you like me to turn you into a human?

46
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:49,800
With this magic ring.

47
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:59,360
I've never cast magic on a wooden puppet with this before. It only works on lazy people, after all. I don't really like working much.

48
00:04:59,510 --> 00:05:01,440
No, let's try casting it.

49
00:05:02,715 --> 00:05:04,720
Do as I say...

50
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:08,920
This and that...

51
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:15,560
Village, museum...

52
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,340
(Fast-forwarding)

53
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:38,320
Pinch yourself.

54
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:39,580
Huh?

55
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,000
Ow!

56
00:05:42,295 --> 00:05:44,040
It really hurts!

57
00:05:44,365 --> 00:05:46,900
It worked. Now eat this.

58
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:48,460
Huh?

59
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:55,100
It's delicious! Is meat really this good?

60
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:09,580
Huh? Suddenly it doesn't taste good anymore.

61
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:13,660
You turned back into a wooden puppet.

62
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:17,420
Please, Boss! Make me human again!

63
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:21,800
I'll be your servant, I'll do anything! Please, Boss!

64
00:06:23,055 --> 00:06:25,300
Only if you bring me a hundred gold coins.

65
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,340
I don't have that kind of money!

66
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:31,120
Then bring me the old bastard who made you.

67
00:06:31,565 --> 00:06:32,600
Grandpa?

68
00:06:33,055 --> 00:06:37,340
That's right. Do that, and I'll make you human. Grandpa?

69
00:06:49,090 --> 00:06:51,340
Mokku, do you want something?

70
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:53,750
G-Grandpa?

71
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:56,300
Mokku, what is the matter?

72
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:59,620
I want to become human, no matter what!

73
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:04,560
A Gypsy in the forest cast a spell on me earlier, and I became human!

74
00:07:05,710 --> 00:07:09,620
That's ridiculous! Magic can't turn you into a human!

75
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:14,280
It's true! It hurt when I pinched myself, and I even got to eat meat!

76
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:23,540
But the wizard said he won't cast any more magic unless I bring a hundred gold coins or bring Grandpa to him.

77
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:31,360
But I could never do that. Grandpa is too precious to me.

78
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:36,540
Still... I really want to eat meat like that again.

79
00:07:39,970 --> 00:07:42,820
If it's what you wish for, I'll do anything.

80
00:07:42,970 --> 00:07:45,440
Really? Truly?

81
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,400
Yes, truly. Come here.

82
00:07:50,580 --> 00:07:51,620
Grandpa!

83
00:07:52,775 --> 00:07:56,900
It's all right, it's all right. In return, you must be a good boy.

84
00:08:05,550 --> 00:08:10,620
I'll work hard and save up a hundred gold coins real fast, and come get you!

85
00:08:11,490 --> 00:08:19,360
Make sure you sleep under a blanket at night. If you're ever in trouble, go ask your teacher or the priest for help.

86
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,560
Okay.

87
00:08:20,910 --> 00:08:22,900
All right, old man, time to go.

88
00:08:23,715 --> 00:08:25,100
Mokku, take care of yourself.

89
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,180
You take care too, Grandpa!

90
00:08:29,510 --> 00:08:30,510
Yes, yes.

91
00:08:31,925 --> 00:08:32,925
Hyah!

92
00:08:42,709 --> 00:08:44,940
Grandpa! Goodbye!

93
00:08:53,959 --> 00:08:55,620
He's gone...

94
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:57,940
It hurts!

95
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:01,260
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!

96
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:02,820
It really hurts!

97
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,740
It hurts!

98
00:09:07,229 --> 00:09:08,320
It hurts so much!

99
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:09,640
That hurts!

100
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:15,460
It hurts... It really hurts...

101
00:09:22,109 --> 00:09:24,860
I'm a human now. I can eat anything!

102
00:09:25,470 --> 00:09:29,040
Now, where's something to eat...?

103
00:09:33,290 --> 00:09:34,420
Time to eat!

104
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:41,420
Gross... Did Grandpa really eat stuff this awful...?

105
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:48,000
Hey, Mokku! What have you done? You sold Grandfather, didn't you?!

106
00:09:49,989 --> 00:09:52,220
Grandpa said he wanted to go himself!

107
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:57,660
You ungrateful brat! Do you really think you can survive on your own without Grandfather? Well, Mokku?!

108
00:09:57,990 --> 00:10:01,920
Shut up! I'm the master of this house now! Get out! Get out!

109
00:10:01,921 --> 00:10:05,120
It's not too late! Go and bring Grandfather back right now!

110
00:10:06,529 --> 00:10:08,060
Mind your own business! Get out!

111
00:10:08,715 --> 00:10:13,520
You can't even fry an egg! You'll starve and end up a beggar!

112
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:17,000
Beggar or not, who cares as long as I get to eat delicious food?!

113
00:10:17,225 --> 00:10:18,225
You busybody!

114
00:10:20,214 --> 00:10:25,580
Right, it still hurts... Good grief, don't come crying to me when everything goes wrong!

115
00:10:29,069 --> 00:10:32,700
What are you talking about? The fun is just getting started.

116
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:41,600
Grandpa isn't here and I'm really hungry. Please, can I just have one piece of candy?

117
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:49,420
What? The only people entitled to charity are the elderly and the sick. If you want candy, go earn it.

118
00:10:50,075 --> 00:10:52,120
But I'm just a kid!

119
00:10:52,874 --> 00:10:56,060
Even a kid can do some simple chores.

120
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:58,660
Help me out with my work, and I'll give you some candy.

121
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:02,160
You're just saying that so you can make me work for free, mister!

122
00:11:02,455 --> 00:11:03,520
No way!

123
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:07,880
Then suit yourself! It serves a lazy brat like you right to go hungry!

124
00:11:09,015 --> 00:11:11,360
Cheapskate! You're just stingy!

125
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:12,500
What?!

126
00:11:16,399 --> 00:11:18,860
What a rotten kid, when you're the one who's lazy!

127
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:32,500
Being human is so lame. You can't eat anything unless you work.

128
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:42,180
I'm never going to work.

129
00:11:43,499 --> 00:11:46,020
Mokku, haven't you learned your lesson yet?

130
00:11:49,819 --> 00:11:51,300
W-What's wrong, Mokku?

131
00:11:52,909 --> 00:11:53,909
*Gasp!*

132
00:11:55,409 --> 00:11:56,960
Stop! Those are poisonous berries!

133
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:58,140
Shut up!

134
00:11:58,460 --> 00:12:00,020
Stop! They'll kill you!

135
00:12:00,650 --> 00:12:02,740
Mokku! Those are poison! Stop!

136
00:12:14,210 --> 00:12:16,920
It hurts! My stomach hurts!

137
00:12:18,019 --> 00:12:19,320
Oh, Tonton!

138
00:12:19,345 --> 00:12:21,540
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts so much!

139
00:12:23,329 --> 00:12:25,440
I told you so!

140
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,520
It hurts!

141
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:34,360
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!

142
00:12:37,255 --> 00:12:39,120
Mokku, are you all right?

143
00:12:40,599 --> 00:12:43,940
I don't want to be human anymore! I hate being human!

144
00:12:44,929 --> 00:12:48,620
Mokku, you have not become a real human.

145
00:12:50,039 --> 00:12:51,900
You cannot become human just yet.

146
00:12:52,445 --> 00:12:53,445
Why not?

147
00:12:54,319 --> 00:12:57,460
Because you do not possess a righteous and kind heart.

148
00:12:57,915 --> 00:13:02,460
But I don't want to become human anymore! Nothing good ever comes of it!

149
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:06,620
That is because you do not yet know true joy.

150
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:08,740
True joy?

151
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:16,940
Humans have many kinds of joy. The joy of living, the joy of loving, the joy of working.

152
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:19,800
Is working really that fun?

153
00:13:20,229 --> 00:13:24,040
Yes. But only those who sweat with their own effort can understand it.

154
00:13:24,215 --> 00:13:26,340
Then what should I do?

155
00:13:27,165 --> 00:13:31,420
If you turn the wizard's ring the other way, you can return to being an Oak Tree puppet.

156
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:36,280
And then, you must strive to have a righteous and kind heart.

157
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,160
Do you understand?

158
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:42,940
Ah, wait!

159
00:13:48,689 --> 00:13:49,940
She's gone...

160
00:13:52,135 --> 00:13:54,400
All right! I'll do it! I'll definitely do it!

161
00:13:54,759 --> 00:13:55,980
That's it! That's the spirit!

162
00:13:57,369 --> 00:13:58,369
Wh-Who are you?

163
00:13:59,759 --> 00:14:01,700
I'm Giorgio the crow.

164
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:02,540
Giorgio?

165
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:04,160
Look what showed up.

166
00:14:05,030 --> 00:14:07,020
The Oak Tree Fairy sent me.

167
00:14:07,345 --> 00:14:11,380
You're an enchanted devil, after all. The moment I look away, you get into mischief.

168
00:14:11,645 --> 00:14:16,260
My family's been nesting in that Oak Tree for generations, you know.

169
00:14:16,670 --> 00:14:18,320
So I couldn't say no.

170
00:14:18,445 --> 00:14:20,880
Hmph! I don't need someone like you here anyway!

171
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,760
I'm not a devil!

172
00:14:23,605 --> 00:14:27,120
The proof that you're a devil is that you have no empathy for others.

173
00:14:27,335 --> 00:14:29,580
When you act like that, take this!

174
00:14:31,660 --> 00:14:32,660
Serves you right.

175
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:37,520
Listen, Mokku. If you get any bad ideas from now on, I won't hesitate to peck you.

176
00:14:38,105 --> 00:14:39,360
That's so mean!

177
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:45,380
This is great. I think I'll leave things to Giorgio the crow for a bit and take a rest.

178
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:51,860
(Magical Marker)

179
00:15:01,895 --> 00:15:04,520
All right, here is the sorcerer's house.

180
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:07,720
It looks kind of scary... Are you whining again?

181
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:10,720
Ouch!

182
00:15:11,070 --> 00:15:12,460
Here I go!

183
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:15,620
Huh?

184
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,380
Oh, they look just like me.

185
00:15:22,249 --> 00:15:24,760
And they're all a bit strange.

186
00:15:26,959 --> 00:15:27,980
What did you come here for?!

187
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:36,900
What do you want?!

188
00:15:37,739 --> 00:15:42,400
Please give Grandpa back! And please turn me back into a wooden puppet!

189
00:15:42,825 --> 00:15:44,860
Did you bring the 100 gold coins?

190
00:15:46,209 --> 00:15:50,060
But I didn't want to be a devil! I wanted to be human!

191
00:15:50,735 --> 00:15:51,735
What did you say?

192
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:56,860
I never asked to be made into a devil! Now give me back my Grandpa!

193
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:58,280
Shut your mouth!

194
00:15:58,615 --> 00:15:59,615
Let go of me!

195
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:04,740
Cheeky little brat. Bruno, take him to the old man and make him help out!

196
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:08,020
Make them churn out defective puppets!

197
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:11,680
Move it!

198
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:19,860
(Grandpa... Grandpa...)

199
00:16:19,861 --> 00:16:20,861
Oh!

200
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:23,640
Mokku!

201
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:24,680
Grandpa!

202
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:28,340
Old man, Mokku is your assistant now. Work him to the bone!

203
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:29,820
Mokku!

204
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:31,860
Grandpa, I'm so sorry...

205
00:16:32,575 --> 00:16:36,820
I missed you. I was worried sick about you...

206
00:16:38,429 --> 00:16:49,040
Grandpa, they turned me into a devil... Is that so? I've been locked up here too, forced to do this awful work. What are we going to do?

207
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:54,300
There's nothing an old man like me can do... I never should have come here...

208
00:16:56,589 --> 00:17:05,480
What's the matter? Don't worry, Grandpa. I'll definitely save you!

209
00:17:05,679 --> 00:17:07,520
And then I'll turn back into a normal puppet!

210
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:21,040
Now!

211
00:17:21,239 --> 00:17:24,099
Do it right!

212
00:17:30,519 --> 00:17:33,860
If I turn that ring backward, I can turn back into a puppet!

213
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:41,280
Take that!

214
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:14,700
This will do it!

215
00:18:15,524 --> 00:18:16,524
I did it!

216
00:18:16,814 --> 00:18:18,140
All right, pinch me!

217
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,540
It doesn't hurt, does it?

218
00:18:20,905 --> 00:18:22,200
Now I'm back to being a puppet!

219
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:23,420
Hurray!

220
00:18:28,289 --> 00:18:32,140
Thank goodness, Mokku. But I'm staying here.

221
00:18:32,284 --> 00:18:34,140
Why? Why, Grandpa?

222
00:18:34,484 --> 00:18:42,420
I was the one who made those defective puppets. I can't just run away.
But if you stay here, they'll just force you to make more defective puppets!

223
00:18:43,164 --> 00:18:47,880
I will never make puppets like that again. Now, go back to the village on your own.

224
00:18:48,839 --> 00:18:51,060
If you're not going, Grandpa, I'm staying too.

225
00:18:51,469 --> 00:18:55,180
You can't do that. If you stay in a place like this, they'll put a spell on you again.

226
00:18:55,594 --> 00:18:57,720
I can't go back and leave you behind, Grandpa!

227
00:18:59,154 --> 00:19:03,300
Mokku...
I know I'm a bad boy, but I love you most of all, Grandpa.

228
00:19:04,205 --> 00:19:08,181
Mokku... Mokku...
Grandpa.

229
00:19:09,849 --> 00:19:14,120
Boss, starting today, I'll do anything—begging, stealing, whatever it takes!

230
00:19:14,774 --> 00:19:17,960
All right, good attitude. Go make us some real money.

231
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:20,105
Yes, sir.
That's strange.

232
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:21,960
Don't worry about it.

233
00:19:27,389 --> 00:19:30,200
Mokku, just like you said, I brought my friends!

234
00:19:30,524 --> 00:19:32,540
Thank you. Now listen, everyone.

235
00:19:33,559 --> 00:19:38,000
From now on, if you do anything bad at all, this crow will peck your butts.

236
00:19:38,629 --> 00:19:41,620
But if we don't bring in any money, the boss will whip us!

237
00:19:41,979 --> 00:19:46,580
I'll take the beatings for you. I'm made of oak, so it doesn't hurt me at all.

238
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:54,280
No way! The boss is way too scary! (children chattering)

239
00:19:54,281 --> 00:19:57,200
Aaargh! Ow, ow, ow!!

240
00:19:57,201 --> 00:19:58,760
It hurts...

241
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:00,080
(children chattering)

242
00:20:00,081 --> 00:20:03,080
Ow, ow, ow, ow!!

243
00:20:03,081 --> 00:20:04,920
Ow!! All right, stop!

244
00:20:05,259 --> 00:20:07,060
Good, that should be enough!

245
00:20:09,214 --> 00:20:10,720
Got that, everyone?!

246
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:13,080
(children chattering)

247
00:20:15,199 --> 00:20:18,620
What do you mean you didn't bring in any money?!

248
00:20:18,669 --> 00:20:20,360
You lazy bums!!

249
00:20:20,509 --> 00:20:24,960
I'm the one who took everyone away. Beat only m— - Ow! - You bastard!

250
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:26,780
- Ow! - You bastard!

251
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:29,940
- Ow! - Ow!

252
00:20:29,941 --> 00:20:30,520
- Ow! - Ow!

253
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:33,360
- Take that! - Ow!

254
00:20:33,685 --> 00:20:34,685
- Ow! - Ow!

255
00:20:35,159 --> 00:20:36,180
- Ow! - Ow!

256
00:20:38,559 --> 00:20:40,880
Starting tomorrow, you better do whatever dirty work it takes to bring in cash!

257
00:20:41,069 --> 00:20:43,560
Steal, pick pockets, do whatever it takes!

258
00:20:44,354 --> 00:20:45,880
- All right! - All right!

259
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:55,680
(stomach rumbles)

260
00:20:58,114 --> 00:21:02,380
You damn fool! How many days has it been since you brought in any money?!

261
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:06,460
Ow! It hurts! Ow!

262
00:21:22,179 --> 00:21:25,640
They must be wearing down by now. Yeah, time to make our move.

263
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:34,980
I've praised you over ten times today, yet you didn't earn a thing! If you want good food and booze, you should work for it yourself!

264
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:41,420
What did you say?! Say that again!
If you're starving because you won't work, it's your own fault!

265
00:21:41,655 --> 00:21:44,120
W-Why, you little...!

266
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:49,660
Now!

267
00:21:52,769 --> 00:21:53,769
Salari!

268
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:56,300
The magic ring!

269
00:21:56,380 --> 00:21:57,380
Crow, wait!

270
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:59,020
Give back the ring!

271
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:04,800
Without that ring, the spell will break!

272
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:06,480
It worked! Now then!

273
00:22:21,919 --> 00:22:26,760
Grandpa, those puppets were only moving because of magic, weren't they?

274
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:33,920
When I made you, I poured all my love into it. Magic alone isn't enough.

275
00:22:45,014 --> 00:22:53,940
"Spare some change, please..." People who try to take the easy way out without working always end up like that. Yeah, starting tomorrow, I'll work too.

276
00:22:54,554 --> 00:22:56,240
That's the spirit.

277
00:22:56,524 --> 00:22:57,524
Grandpa?

278
00:22:57,980 --> 00:22:58,360
Hmm?

279
00:22:58,674 --> 00:22:59,960
I'm tired.

280
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:05,600
Didn't you just say you were going to work? But my legs are completely worn out, I really can't move!

281
00:23:05,820 --> 00:23:06,420
Carry me on your back.

282
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:08,000
What am I going to do with you...

283
00:23:08,185 --> 00:23:10,240
All right. Heave-ho.

284
00:23:13,199 --> 00:23:15,900
Kind sirs to my left and right...

285
00:23:16,664 --> 00:23:21,080
Please spare some charity, have pity on a poor...

286
00:23:33,229 --> 00:23:35,880
Mokku runs around shouting at the top of his lungs for the whole town to hear.

287
00:23:36,849 --> 00:23:42,440
Mokku frightens everyone with endless lies, claiming there is a monster in the forest or that a house is on fire.

288
00:23:43,629 --> 00:23:48,620
To punish Mokku, the Oak Tree Fairy makes his nose grow longer and longer.

289
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:57,120
Desperate to get his nose back to normal, Mokku promises to be a good boy, but will he be able to keep that promise to the very end?

290
00:23:57,600 --> 00:24:00,080
Look forward to next week's Kashi no Ki Mokku!

